-- title:
--   Automorphisms of the crossing model rescale V by a unit
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring: a commutative ring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal. Let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, let $e \geq 1$ be a natural number, and write $M =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C(\varpi^{e})$, i.e. $M = W[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^{e})$, with $U$ and $V$ the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$ and $\mathrm{const}(w)$ the class of the constant series $C(w)$. Let $\theta : M \to M$ be a ring isomorphism of $M$ with itself such that $\theta(\mathrm{const}(\varpi)) = \mathrm{const}(\varpi)$ and such that $\theta(U)$ does not lie in the ideal of $M$ generated by the two elements $V$ and $\mathrm{const}(\varpi)$. The assertion is that there exists $t \in M$ which is a unit and satisfies $\theta(V) = t \cdot V$.
--
--   This is the presentation-independence step for the crossing (node) model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^{e})$ describing the local structure of a modular curve at a point of the special fibre where two branches meet: an automorphism fixing the uniformiser and not carrying the $U$-branch into the $V$-branch preserves the ideal $(V)$ up to a unit factor. It is used in the analysis of the behaviour of $j$-like coordinates on blow-up charts at linked Hasse points, and in the accompanying statement about the order of the induced tangent action.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_isUnit_apply_V_eq_mul_V_of_ringEquiv_apply_const_eq_of_apply_U_not_mem_span.lean

